{"episodes":{"211221":"Dust Devil in Tucson Metro caused a 9 inch diameter tree branch to be broken. No injuries or fatalities associated with this dust devil.","211263":"Showers and weak thunderstorms generated high winds across portions of central and north central South Dakota from the afternoon of April 22nd into the early morning hours of April 23rd. A peak wind gust of 71 mph was recorded at the Sand Lake RAWS 13 miles east northeast of Eureka, and at the South Dakota Department of Transportation mesonet station 5 miles north of Reliance. Winds were strong enough 5 miles east of Pollock to flatten a 10 by 10 outbuilding and gazebo, and power poles were snapped 6 miles north northeast of Eureka, with a loss of power to 615 customers. Power outages were also reported in Walworth county to 108 customers. The lightning overnight sparked a 30 acre fire near the town of Barnard in Brown county.","211383":"Video showed a well-developed landspout tornado northeast of Donovan just west of the Illinois Indiana state line that persisted for several minutes.","211406":"Scattered thunderstorms developed during the afternoon hours along a frontal boundary situated across central Ohio.","211414":"Ahead of a strong low pressure system, hot temperatures, just enough humid air, and an unstable atmosphere, created widespread showers and scattered thunderstorms, some of which included severe wind gusts for many locations.","211681":"Isolated severe storms developed over portions of SE Texas. These storms produced extensive damage to utility lines across Jackson County.","211809":"Another Spring storm brought mountain snow, rain and thunderstorms to the area from April 20th through April 22nd. There were numerous reports of roadway flooding due to heavy rain and thunderstorms. There was also a report of a rock slide on State Route 16 from the heavy rain with rocks all over the road. Moderate mountain snow brought periods of chain controls over the mountain highways.","212840":"Discrete severe thunderstorms developed off of Lake Michigan and tracked southeast producing a few reports of quarter-sized hail.","212841":"Discrete severe thunderstorms developed off of Lake Michigan, tracked southeast, and congealed into multicell clusters. Along the way, storms produced quarter-sized hail. Most reports of quarter-size hail came from Putnam County, Ohio.","213237":"Heavy rainfall along the Blue mountain foothills and across the Blue mountains resulted in flooding along the Umatilla river.","213343":"Severe thunderstorms developed and moved across western SD and brought strong, damaging wind gusts to the Black Hills. Storms consolidated into a line and produced strong wind gusts further east."},"events":[{"begin":"2026-04-22T00:41Z","county":"Sacramento","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2026-04-22T07:41Z","endLat":38.4911,"endLon":-121.1468,"episode":211809,"id":1331070,"injuries":0,"lat":38.49,"location":"0.88 SE Cosumne","lon":-121.16,"narrative":"California Highway Patrol reported river and roadway flooding on the bridge at Highway 16 and Kiefer Boulevard.","source":"Law Enforcement","state":"CA","type":"Flood","wfo":"STO"},{"begin":"2026-04-22T02:46Z","county":"Tehama","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2026-04-22T07:46Z","endLat":39.9095,"endLon":-122.127,"episode":211809,"id":1331071,"injuries":0,"lat":39.91,"location":"3.25 ESE Corning","lon":-122.12,"narrative":"California Highway Patrol reported roadway flooding across both lanes on South Avenue at Hall Road.","source":"Law Enforcement","state":"CA","type":"Flood","wfo":"STO"},{"begin":"2026-04-22T02:50Z","county":"Sacramento","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2026-04-22T07:50Z","endLat":38.6078,"endLon":-121.2691,"episode":211809,"id":1331072,"injuries":0,"lat":38.61,"location":"0.69 S Citrus","lon":-121.27,"narrative":"California Highway Patrol reported roadway flooding on the Highway 50 westbound 